WEBVTT

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.290
We're going ahead, Nagisa.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.150
The assassin from Dotsuku Zone

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.770
used Zakenna to possess Yuka's 
shadow, and attack us.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.360
I won't let someone who uses cowardly 
tactics like that to get the better of me.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.310
We'll have to put some spirit into 
it, and do our best to fight back.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.330
Do your best.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.390
Why don't you encourage 
him in a louder voice?

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.770
Honoka!

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:03.050
If you don't say it louder, 
Fujimura-kun can't hear you.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.230
What are you saying?

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.020
I wasn't saying it to him...

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.590
Nagisa... Are you free tomorrow?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.550
Tomorrow?

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.940
I'm going to help with the 
harvesting at a friend's farm,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.290
so I wanted to come, and help.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.140
Sure.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.400
I'm so glad.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.330
I'm sure Fujimura-kun will be 
happy that you're coming, too.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.820
He asked me to help.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.830
His friend, Kimata's grandfather is a farmer,

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.620
and he asked him to come, and 
help them harvest the vegetables.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.550
Of course, Fujimura-kun will be there, too.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.490
See you tomorrow.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.100
Farm work with Fujimura-san?

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.980
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.780
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.620
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.890
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.860
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.730
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.630
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.540
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.140
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.940
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.050
<i>become stronger</i>

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.820
<i>and closer</i>

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.820
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.390
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.560
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.430
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:36.700
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.600
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.300
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.110
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:46.010
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.580
<i>Together we are</i>

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.650
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.080
What should I wear tomorrow?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.450
I told you to knock before you come in!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.920
You have all your clothes out...

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.000
Is it for a date?

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.610
Of course not!

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.710
I'm going to help out at a 
farm with Honoka tomorrow.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.430
You're going to a farm?

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.840
Why are you concentrating so hard

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.540
on picking out your clothes 
just to go to a farm?

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.810
Because...

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.940
What am I thinking?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.540
No way! No way!

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.030
Mom! Something's wrong with Sis!

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:42.420
Lately, I've had my doubts about letting 
Nagisa continue to look after me mepo.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:50.840
"CAPTURE HIS HEART! 
HEART-THROBBING FARM WORK"

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.850
Thank you all for coming all the 
way out here to help, everybody.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:24.370
Grandpa hurt his shoulder, and I 
couldn't handle all the work myself.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:27.790
I told you I'm fine!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.430
The doctor told you not 
to overdo it, didn't he?

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.110
I hate doctors.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.280
You should take it easy 
once in a while, Grandpa.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.920
His grandfather's stubborn, isn't he?

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.770
Do all of these fields belong 
to you, Grandma Kimata?

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.930
That's right.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:58.060
That's why I want you all to 
harvest lots of vegetables.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.790
All right. I'll work with my grandma...

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.700
Fujimura-kun and Nagisa are both 
athletes, so you make a good pair.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.910
It's okay with me.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.120
Kiriya-kun... You'll work with me, okay?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.830
Fujimura-san...

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.820
Just come right out, and say 
what you want to say to him.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:17.710
Misumi-san...

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:19.890
Shall we go?

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:37.110
What I want to say to him...?

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.330
What should I say?

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.400
What am I going to do?

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:51.690
Misumi-san... That's awesome.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.060
You're really good at that, aren't you?

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.160
When did I do all that?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:03.280
There are girls who don't like to do work 
that's harsh and dirty like this, aren't there?

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.030
It's not that I don't 
understand their feelings,

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.260
but I have to give you credit, Misumi-san.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.970
Did he just praise me?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.260
Did he really praise me?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:26.380
Cabbage is a plant that originally comes from

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.280
the coastal regions of western 
and southern Europe...

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.700
They're part of the same group 
as broccoli, cauliflower,

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.210
kale and Brussels sprouts.

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.400
At the beginning, it was a plant like 
spinach that wouldn't grow round.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:43.240
Kiriya-kun... When you finish 
over there, you can...

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:56.080
Kiriya-kun! You mustn't goof off like that.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.860
Everyone else is working hard.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.780
What good will it do to work hard?

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.330
With so much cabbage, there's 
no way we can do it.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.930
It's impossible to do it alone...

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:10.040
That's why we're all putting our efforts 
together to try and get it done.

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.270
Humans are weak, aren't they?

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:19.660
You can't do anything unless you all put 
your efforts together, and work together.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:23.370
It's because we all put our efforts 
together that make people strong.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.060
What do you mean?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.980
Just do it, and you'll understand.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.860
Come on, and help me.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.020
Cabbage... cabbage...

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.500
Why do they keep growing so much of this?

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:51.210
What good will it do us to do this anyway?

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:56.440
The cabbage that we're harvesting 
will go to the market,

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.840
and then to the vegetable 
stands and the supermarkets,

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:01.190
and finally end up as a 
part of everyone's meal.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.050
What a bother.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:05.400
Humans are so strange.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.910
Move your hands instead of your mouth.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:13.380
Honoka! Kiriya! Let's have lunch.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.200
Coming!

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:15.990
Wait!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.870
Why?

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.250
Go ahead, and eat.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:24.080
We'll work a little longer 
before we have lunch.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.400
All right.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.250
Why?

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.480
You have to make up for goofing off earlier.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.900
We can do that later.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:33.800
No, we can't!

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:34.950
Kiriya-kun!

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:39.300
Honoka hates to do things halfway.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:43.520
Even though Kiriya-kun's angry, 
Honoka's really working him to death.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.480
That's what's so scary about Honoka.

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.950
That's not true!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:53.290
Honoka scolds him because 
she's thinking of him.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.670
I think that's what's good about Honoka.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.080
Thank you.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.780
As her childhood friend, 
I was worried about her.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:07.520
That others wouldn't like 
that she's so strict...

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:12.670
So I'm happy that she has a 
friend who understands her.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.460
Misumi-san...?

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.870
There's no tea left, so 
I'm going to get more.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:33.210
Why is it that when I'm with 
Fujimura-san, I can't say anything...?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.730
Mepple! You love me this 
much, don't you mipo?

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.810
Of course mepo!

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.280
What is this?

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.810
It's the Prism Love Checker mepo.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.470
Prism Love Checker?

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:59.500
If the two of you each 
touch these buttons here,

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.840
it will measure how much 
you love each other mipo.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.600
You do it like this mepo.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:14.220
The more lamps that light up on the meter,

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.270
the more you love each other mepo.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.670
In the Field of Light,

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:20.800
we always used this to confirm 
our love for each other mepo.

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:22.780
And it always came out love love mipo.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.220
Let me borrow this for a little while.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.450
Are you going to use it 
on that boy, Fuji-P mepo?

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.850
Nagisa loves Fuji-P... Don't you mipo?

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:35.610
No, I don't!

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.210
Fujimura-san is Honoka's childhood friend,

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:41.710
so it's not good if he didn't like me...

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:45.640
I'm just going to use it to check that out.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.350
I wonder if Nagisa's embarrassed mipo.

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:52.910
Nagisa's just not aware 
that she's in love mepo.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:56.090
She's so childish I don't know 
what to do with her mepo.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:59.120
If I use this, even if I don't say anything,

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.970
I'll know if Fujimura-san likes me or not.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.070
All we have to do is touch this together...

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.120
I really am a coward, aren't I?

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.140
Where are you going, Grandma Kimata?

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:39.830
It's gotten a little cold, so I'm going 
to take out a jacket for Grandpa.

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:44.610
He can't do anything by himself.

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.260
I know! I'll try this out!

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.740
Your shoulder will get cold, Grandpa.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:15.820
I don't want it.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:17.620
Excuse me...

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.880
Will the two of you touch this for me?

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.310
I pass.

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:26.710
Grandpa!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.940
It's so bright and cheery. This is fun!

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:42.070
The lamps all lit up!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.930
What happens after this, Nagisa?

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:50.250
That's all.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.250
How useless!

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.510
Grandpa!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.680
What's wrong with saying that 
something is useless is useless?

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.210
You're being rude to Nagisa.

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.980
I'm so sorry.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:02.620
I'll give this back.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.090
It doesn't work.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:09.000
The Prism Love Checker is always right mepo!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.560
Does that couple look like 
they're in love to you?

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:15.040
No way!

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.090
I can't handle this.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.860
Carry this, Kiriya-kun!

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:33.650
Kiriya-kun!

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.360
After all the trouble we 
went through to pack it up.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.750
Are you okay, Kiriya-kun?

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:41.510
Oh no!

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.120
It's just a scratch.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.130
We have to take care of it. Come with me.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.780
What about the cabbage?

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:50.190
We'll take care of the cut first.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.790
I wouldn't even call this a cut.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.170
Even if it's just a small cut,

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:00.080
the bacteria gets into it, 
it might get infected.

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:02.450
Why?

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:07.050
Why do you treat someone else's cut?

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.980
I can't just ignore someone 
who's hurt, can I?

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:14.560
Are all people like that?

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.130
Yes, they are.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:26.130
I'm so glad I brought some bandages.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.460
Let's finish the rest.

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:32.920
Since you hurt your finger, 
I'll carry the boxes.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:55.020
Thank you, everyone. Let's have tea.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.510
We'll clean up first.

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.020
Where's Kiriya-kun?

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:02.270
He was here a minute ago.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:06.430
We finished it all.

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:10.690
That's right...

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:15.660
It's because we all put our efforts 
together that makes people strong.

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.960
It's not like you, Kiriya.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:22.940
You're wide open.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.750
If I had the mind to do it, you'd be dead.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.530
Poisonny.

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.530
I hope I'm wrong,

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.930
but don't tell me that in your attempt 
to gain favor with the humans,

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:35.490
they've gained your favor instead?

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.940
You know that would never happen!

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:38.810
Oh, really?

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.680
Then why are you getting so upset about it?

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.150
You're going to get them, aren't you?

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:44.150
I'll help you.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.230
Go, Zakenna!

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:00.480
Zakenna!

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:17.560
Is it an earthquake?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.850
Who's afraid of a little earthquake?

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.190
It's strange for an earthquake, isn't it?

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:26.150
Zakenna!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.570
Zakenna!

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:43.750
Grandpa!

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.910
Zakenna!

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.760
You monster!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.950
Zakenna!

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.560
Zakenna!

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:58.700
Zakenna!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.450
Over here, you monster!

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:17.720
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:47.850
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:50.730
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.430
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.950
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:01.390
Go back to where you came from!

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.170
There's no one here!

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:05.410
Let's go after them!

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.710
Zakenna!

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:14.420
Zakenna...!

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.590
Zakenna!

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:34.960
White!

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.790
White...!

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.930
Welcome, Young Lady!

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.570
Will you hand over the Prism Stones?

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.330
I refuse!

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.970
Zakenna!

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:09.280
You people have a fatal flaw.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:12.090
You can't do anything alone.

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:16.250
It's no good mepo.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.860
It's not an ordinary rock mepo.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:20.680
There's a powerful force behind it.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.280
I'm not giving up!

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.710
I'll ask you again.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:32.450
Hand over the Prism Stones, Young Lady.

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.030
I'll never hand them over to you!

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.490
Then it can't be helped...

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.920
Zakenna!

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.190
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:51.130
Black!

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.100
Your hero is here.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:57.850
You mean heroine, don't you?

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:00.770
Let's get rid of them.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.870
Black Thunder!

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:06.280
White Thunder!

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:15.260
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.940
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:22.450
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

